A||||9||rockcrawl||Need pics/info on 88 rear swaybar||||1||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||10-20-2001||06:37 PM||||I have a rear swaybar for an '88, and an '88 coupe cradle. I just cannot figure out where the bar is supposed to mount on the cradle, and where the endlinks mount on the suspension bits. From memory I think the bar should mount on top of the cradle?? Pictures would be great, but any info greatly appreciated.<P>Jon||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||10-20-2001||07:01 PM||||The bar does go on top of the cradle on the 88 but you also need the 2 brackets that go on the shock lower mounting point. They're "L" shaped brackets that go on the 2 big bolts||||reg||1
Z||000002||qwikgta||10-21-2001||11:21 PM||||Rock... I just did this last weekend, yes the bar mounts to the top of the cradle, I had to get mine in through the engine bay.  I only have a 2.5 so there was room to do it.  It looked to me that you would have to take some of the suspension parts off to get it in any other way.  The endlinks mount to two brackes that mount to the struts.  They face the front of the car and are marked L and R.  The best pic I could find is on page 247 of the Chiltons guide.  It shows the mounting points for the swaybar and how to do it on the strut.  All 88 have the holes for it and even have the correct holes in the fenderwell dirt covers.<P>Good luck<P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||10-22-2001||06:53 AM||||Thanks guys, The problem is that I was looking at a non-GT cradle thinking they were all the same. It turns out the GT cradle has extra brackets welded on for swaybar mounting. ||||reg||7
Z||000004||Phil||10-22-2001||07:14 AM||||Just looked at my Formula cradle(sitting on the garage floor) and nothing is welded in place. The 2 pivot blocks bolt to the uprights by the rear cradle bolts and the end links go to the 2 brackets bolted to the struts.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||10-22-2001||06:58 PM||||Phil, are you sure that's a stock bar locaton? I have an '88 GT here and the bar is missing, but I can see where there are two mounting pads on the cradle for the pivot blocks. These mounting pads are welded to the front of the cradle where the main rails meet the forward crossmember. They appear to be stock and they are not on the '88 coupe cradle. And yes, it does have the endlink brackets on the struts.||||reg||7
Z||000006||skitime||10-22-2001||07:23 PM||||Hey you go Rockcrawl,  88 Cradle and sway bar pics.  BTW I need the links for this if anyone has a pair.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pa220009.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pa220010.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rockcrawl||10-22-2001||07:56 PM||||Thanks again guys! Upon further inspection I found the mounting holes on both cradles. The welded-on pads I saw were added when the cradle was hactchetized...er.. I mean modified for a V8. And then when the hatchet...I mean modified cradle was put back into the car the bar had to be removed due to clearance problems. I've got it all figured out now, I promise.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rockcrawl||10-22-2001||07:58 PM||||Hey Skitime, why does it appear as if there's still a 2.8 sitting in that cradle? Have you been napping!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000009||skitime||10-22-2001||08:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>Hey Skitime, why does it appear as if there's still a 2.8 sitting in that cradle? Have you been napping!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You know why the 2.8 is still in there.  I am waiting for you to help with the 3800SC.  I really would like to have a schematic of the wiring harness you reduced for Chads car.  Bottom line is I could definitely use you advise and or help.  Hope the pics helped.<P>||||reg||1
